        {
          "id": "SP_STAUROTHECA_GRACILIS_PE_A_CANTERO_2017",
          "name": "Staurotheca gracilis Peña Cantero, 2017",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Staurotheca",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "(Holotype). Stem 60 mm high (Fig. 3 B), basally polysiphonic, irregularly branched in approximately one plane. Branches narrow at origin (Fig. 10 D), basally more or less perpendicular to previous one, strongly curving upwards later. Branches repeatedly branched (up to sixth order present) (Fig. 3 B), with anastomose. A few perisarc constrictions irregularly distributed along stem and branches. Hydrothecae typically arranged in decussate verticils of three, resulting in six longitudinal rows of hydrothecae. Decussate pairs also present in some parts (Fig. 10 D). Hydrotheca elongate (Fig. 10 D – H), roughly cylindrical, almost completely adnate to branch, and with mushroom-shaped diaphragm. Measurements (in µm). Hydrothecae: abcauline wall 700 – 800, free part of adcauline wall 30 – 60, adnate part of adcauline wall 800 – 930, adcauline wall 830 – 980, diameter at aperture 230 – 260, maximum diameter 330 – 350, diameter at diaphragm 300 – 310. Cnidome: larger microbasic mastigophores 22 – 24 x 5 – 6, smaller microbasic mastigophores 9 x 2.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9327209",
          "sourceIds": {
